{"crc":"60a6a165","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is in the `FigureCanvasMac.resize` method in `backend_macosx.py`. When a figure is unpickled, the `resize` method is called, and it's dividing by `self.device_pixel_ratio` which causes the DPI to double on M1 Macs.\n\nThe issue is that `device_pixel_ratio` is not properly initialized when the canvas is created during unpickling. The fix should ensure that `device_pixel_ratio` is properly set to 1.0 when the canvas is initialized.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_macosx.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n=======\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n        self.device_pixel_ratio = 1.0\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQ9NHXHE7VPZQ918V962SRG","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQ9NHXCG9R3A1D662HS9G16"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786414551.223818}
{"crc":"a91406d2","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:4d576dfc5e99c6616d781168a715511f2a566c427931e5362155d710a9b61331","instance":"01KZQ9NM5Q91HQMPKJ6MQW4J6D","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is in the `FigureCanvasMac.resize` method in `backend_macosx.py`. When a figure is unpickled, the `resize` method is called, and it's dividing by `self.device_pixel_ratio` which causes the DPI to double on M1 Macs.\n\nThe issue is that `device_pixel_ratio` is not properly initialized when the canvas is created during unpickling. The fix should ensure that `device_pixel_ratio` is properly set to 1.0 when the canvas is initialized.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_macosx.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n=======\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n        self.device_pixel_ratio = 1.0\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"trigger_id":"validate"},"producer":null,"schema":"substrate.TriggerFired@1","seq":15,"t":1786414551.2239082}
